# The two `.reference.py` byte-comparison copies were DELETED on 28 Jul 2026.
# rail.py and qc_episode.py now live in this repo, and the integrity gates
# compare them against git HEAD instead (engine/gitgate.py). The gate uses
# `git status --porcelain`, which applies git's own clean filters, so it is
# immune to the autocrlf conversion that made `-text` necessary here.

# The governing standards moved in from Drive on 27 Jul 2026 and must stay
# BYTE-IDENTICAL to their originals. core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so
# without -text git would rewrite these LF files as CRLF on checkout and the
# byte comparison against Drive would silently fail.
docs/*.md -text
docs/**/*.md -text

# The card template library and the card_check regression fixture, added 28 Jul
# 2026. These are reference artifacts: the golden-file test regenerates EP11's
# and EP12's shipped pages from them and diffs the rendered PNGs, and the fixture
# reproduces EP12's C10 as it stood before the collision fix. Keep them LF so a
# fresh clone measures the same bytes this machine does.
.claude/skills/pp-episode-production/assets/cards/**/*.html -text
.claude/skills/pp-episode-production/scripts/testdata/*.html -text
